+**The sun disc, and why it has its own ceiling.** The dome has no sun sprite - what reads as the
+sun IS the Mie forward-scattering lobe, and its peak is unbounded in the `Sun anisotropy factor`
+by construction. At the shipped `g = -0.997` the peak is about 9.1e7 cd/m2, four stops UNDER the
+real solar disc; at the slider's limit `-0.9999` it is 8.2e10, fifty times over, and that is the
+`+Inf` the writer clamp exists for. `r_SceneReferredSkyPeakLuminance` (default **1.6e9 cd/m2**,
+the disc above the atmosphere) caps the sky pass in UNEXPOSED terms, so the disc means the same
+real brightness at every aperture; `r_SceneReferredWriterClamp` is still applied on top so the
+fp16 target can never be overrun. Read it as a bound on an approximation: capping the Mie lobe at
+disc radiance still spreads solar-disc luminance over degrees. The real cure is a physical
+asymmetry factor plus a real sun sprite, which is a content change and is not shipped.
